bin/
obj/
.vs/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo

# Local runtime state
data/
node_modules/
dist/

# Never commit real secrets. The AI provider is configured per tenant at runtime
# under Admin -> AI Settings and stored write-only in the platform's secret vault.
appsettings.*.local.json
*.env
.env

# The vendored platform packages ARE committed on purpose (.packages/) -- they publish
# only to a feed that needs a PAT, so vendoring is what keeps `dotnet restore` working
# on a bare clone. Do not add .packages/ here.

# Tooling-generated launch profiles, never committed. `dotnet run` and the IDEs write one into
# src/*/Properties/ unasked, and Aspire reads its `applicationUrl` to derive a project resource's
# endpoints -- so a committed one would silently decide which ports the API binds, differently on
# every machine and absent in CI (#79). AppHost.cs passes `launchProfileName: null` so the file
# cannot be read even when it exists; this line keeps it from drifting into a commit as well.
**/Properties/launchSettings.json
